course: dictionary
lesson: 3006
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. The word duster is a good example. «you get a duster, Mole … and try and smarten things up a bit» means a cloth for wiping dust, because the Rat wants the room tidied.
explain: The second example gives more clues. The Mole was spring-cleaning with «brooms, dusters and a pail of whitewash (a white paint for walls)». Brooms and whitewash are for cleaning and painting, so a duster is a cleaning tool too.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then test it. If you put the meaning into the sentence and it still makes sense, you have probably chosen well.
fact: A duster is a cloth for wiping dust off furniture and shelves.
fact: A board duster, or board rubber, is a pad for wiping a chalkboard or whiteboard clean.
fact: In the US and Australia, a duster is a long, light coat worn to keep dust off, especially by riders.
fact: A duster can also be a light housecoat.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is the right one.
exercise: In a Western, the cowboy pulls on his long duster before he rides out. What is a duster here? | A cowboy's hat | *A long, light coat to keep off dust | A rope | A horse blanket
exercise: Ms Patel asks Ben to fetch the board duster. What is it? | A bucket of water | A coat to keep dust off | A feather for tickling the ceiling | *A pad for wiping a whiteboard clean
exercise: «Give the shelves a going-over with a duster.» What is the duster used for? | Drying wet hair | Painting the walls | *Wiping dust off the shelves | Riding a horse across the plains
test: In «the Mole was spring-cleaning with brooms, dusters and a pail of whitewash», what is whitewash? | Dust | Ghost paint | A kind of broom | *A white paint for walls
test: Which meaning of duster fits «you get a duster, Mole … and try and smarten things up a bit»? | *A cloth for wiping dust off furniture | A board duster for the classroom | A housecoat for the morning | A long coat for riding
exam: Which meaning of duster fits «give the shelves a going-over with a duster», and which clue in the sentence helped you choose? | *A cloth for wiping dust, because the shelves need cleaning | A housecoat, because it is a home | A long coat, because shelves are tall | A board duster, because shelves are in a classroom
